IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 9.01 and 9.02: Agreement - Self-Employed Person. Piece er1, layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt). Nothing here is verified against the official text. `src:N` is a line of that file.
-- Instrument: the Regulations, made for subsections 152.02(4) and (6) of the Act (piece ei5: the agreement between a
-- self-employed person and the Commission, its termination and the withdrawal of a notice of termination).
-- Both regulations state a form the individual's notice must take. The correlative of the individual's duty to put it in
-- writing is the Commission's claim to receive it in writing; the effect of a valid notice is the Act's (piece ei5).

§ `Regulation 9.01 - termination of the agreement: notice`

-- src:161 | 9.01 The notice referred to in subsection 152.02(4) of the Act that the individual gives to the Commission to terminate the agreement shall be given in writing.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9.01 (src:161)
-- Plain gloss: the self-employed person who ends their agreement with the Commission must give the Commission written
-- notice. A notice that is not in writing is not the notice the Act speaks of (out of range: subsection 152.02(4) of the
-- Act, piece ei5).
GIVEN `the individual gives the Commission a notice to terminate the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9.01 the notice to terminate the agreement is given in the form the Regulations require` IF
        `the individual gives the Commission a notice to terminate the agreement`
    AND `the notice is given in writing`

§ `Regulation 9.02 - withdrawal of the notice`

-- src:164 | 9.02 The withdrawal of the notice referred to in paragraph 152.02(6)(b) of the Act shall be given to the Commission in writing.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9.02 (src:164)
-- Plain gloss: if the individual takes back their notice of termination (the Act's paragraph 152.02(6)(b), piece ei5),
-- they must give the Commission the withdrawal in writing.
GIVEN `the individual gives the Commission a withdrawal of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the withdrawal is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9.02 the withdrawal of the notice is given in the form the Regulations require` IF
        `the individual gives the Commission a withdrawal of the notice`
    AND `the withdrawal is given in writing`
